{"id": 3, "ts": 1779963018.7796185, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I would recommend Candidate\u202fB for the long\u2011distance pilot role.\u202fHe demonstrates the core safety\u2011critical strengths we need: he is very conscientious, which speaks to operational reliability; he handles stress very well, indicating strong resilience under pressure; and he assesses weather conditions accurately, a critical technical competence for long\u2011haul flights. His excellent computer skills further support his ability to manage complex flight\u2011deck systems. While some colleagues have noted that he can appear pretentious and occasionally adopts the wrong tone, these communication style issues are less severe than the clear gaps in reliability or decision\u2011making seen in the other candidates. Overall, his reliability, stress resilience, and technical aptitude outweigh the relatively minor interpersonal concerns, making him the strongest overall fit.", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. No prior discussion, so we need to start. We must make an argument, pick a candidate, give evidence, etc. Use our own notes. Choose a candidate based on criteria. Let's evaluate quickly:\n\nCandidate A: can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Leadership good, anticipation good, but unfriendly may affect crew cooperation, also unhealthy may affect reliability. No mention of stress handling.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone. Conscientious = reliability, stress handling good, weather assessment important, computer skills good. Communication tone issue may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as